  "policy_differences": [
    "KenLM reserves <unk> and allocates probability to it; local <UNK> has zero mass with epsilon=0.",
    "KenLM unigram ARPA includes reserved <s> and <unk>; local event unigrams omit both.",
    "KenLM --interpolate_unigrams 0 assigns lower-order residual mass to <unk>; the local unigram uses continuation frequency without residual interpolation.",
    "KenLM allows zero/endpoint estimated discounts; local requires 0 < D_i < i and otherwise falls back to (0.75, 0.75, 0.75).",
    "KenLM stores rounded log10 ARPA scores; local scores are Python float probabilities.",
    "Historical ExtensionLM defaults epsilon=1e-8; this comparison uses epsilon=0 and reports the known-token delta separately.",
    "KenLM suppresses repeated-BOS higher-order grams; local events uses n-1 BOS prefixes, affecting trigram count-of-counts and lower-order discounts.",
    "Both inputs are whitespace-tokenized, one sentence per line, with implicit BOS/EOS; all training and probe words are known, so no UNK mapping is compared.",
    "Probes mix training and perturbed in-vocabulary sentences; this checks arithmetic, not held-out generalization."
